Tough topic. Lots of wise management decisions for you to make...

In the past I didn't care much about the monster-categories because
for me it was all just "killed by [a monster]".

But the more I looked into the details the more I'd like the rare
creatures more separated.

E.g. Getting killed by all different guardian Angel is probably worth about
36 ascensions, so it hurts to see all these in one group with monsters you
could meet on DL1.

Some alternatives for the categories are
  - handmade grouping
  - grouping monsters by letter
  - grouping monsters by difficulty
  - grouping monsters by rarity
  - one group for all monsters

I'll post my own string-list for "killed by [a monster]" in a seperate message.

May it inspire you...

